# L §2.5: a key-list variable takes its index from its key positions; x[k] makes k a key of ns, whose keys are
# names, not ints, so `k <= n_max` compares a key of ns with an int: refused at load (L §8.4, LOAD-UNIT).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

index ns = [a1, a2]

input n_max: int
input x[k in ns]: int

ask q: x[k] for k in [a1, a2] where k <= n_max

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n_max = 12
  x[a1] = 1
  x[a2] = 2
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT ...
